# QA M5 BUG (D-075 "Lead-out: once the camera's x reaches to x 16, the
# side camera takes over again"; D-083): the hand-over from the scroll to
# the side camera snaps the camera 105 px in one frame. The solver route
# to frame 4380: Resi jumps out of the Strobl shallows and lands on the
# Strobl quay (4368) near the right clamp (screen x ~242). The scroll
# reaches camera x 3328 (col 208) in step 4373; in step 4374 the side
# camera frames her at its follow line (centre at screen x 144) at once:
# camera x 3328 -> 3433, i.e. the whole picture jumps 105 px (6.5 tiles)
# in one frame, then follows at her speed. Any Resi right of the follow
# line at the hand-over (where the right clamp keeps a player who holds
# RIGHT: up to 99 px right of it) gets this jump; the relaxed run
# (qa_m5_wolfgangsee_relaxed) shows it at 4793 -> 4794.
# The replay format has no camera expectation, so this replay only
# reproduces it; the shots show the two frames (camera x from
# `Game::camera()`: 3328 at 4373, 3433 at 4374). Expected (correct): the
# camera moves on continuously at the hand-over (e.g. it keeps scrolling
# or catches up at a bounded speed until she reaches the follow line).
level  = wolfgangsee
seed   = 1
source = handwritten
expect = deaths=0 state=playing
shots  = 4373:handover_before 4374:handover_after
